  "SCR_TEXT_3358": "* (It's a book labelled&  Monster History Part 6.)&         Read it     Do not\\C",
  "SCR_TEXT_3359": " ",
  "SCR_TEXT_3363": "* Unfortunately^1, monsters are&  not experienced with&  illness./",
  "SCR_TEXT_3364": "* However^1, when monsters are&  about to expire of age^1,&  they lie down^1, immobile./",
  "SCR_TEXT_3365": "* We call this state&  \"Fallen Down.\"/",
  "SCR_TEXT_3366": "* A person who has Fallen&  Down will soon perish./",
  "SCR_TEXT_3367": "* In a way^1, this confusing&  situation was all too&  familiar./%%",
  "SCR_TEXT_3370": "* (You decide not to read it.)/%%",
  "SCR_TEXT_339": "\\E2ï¼Š ã•ã‚^1ã€€&ã€€ ã²ã ã‚Šã®ã‚¹ã‚¤ãƒƒãƒã‚‚&ã€€ ãŠã—ã¦ã¡ã‚‡ã†ã ã„ã€‚/%",
  "SCR_TEXT_3393": "ï¼Š (It's a book labelled&  Monster History Part 7.)&         Read it     Do not\\C",
  "SCR_TEXT_3394": " ",
  "SCR_TEXT_3398": "ï¼Š When a human dies^1, its&  soul remains stable&  outside the body./",
  "SCR_TEXT_3399": "ï¼Š Meanwhile^1, a monster's soul&  disappears near-instantly&  upon death./",
  "SCR_TEXT_3400": "ï¼Š This allows monsters to&  absorb the souls of&  humansâ€¦/",
  "SCR_TEXT_3401": "ï¼Š While it is extremely&  difficult for humans to&  absorb a monster's soul./",
  "SCR_TEXT_3402": "ï¼Š This is why they feared us./",
  "SCR_TEXT_3403": "ï¼Š Though monsters are weak^1,&  with enough human soulsâ€¦/",
  "SCR_TEXT_3404": "ï¼Š They could easily destroy&  all of mankind./%%",
  "SCR_TEXT_3407": "ï¼Š (You decide not to read it.)/%%",
  "SCR_TEXT_3413": "ï¼Š (It's a book labelled&  Monster History Part 8.)&         Read it     Do not\\C",
  "SCR_TEXT_3414": " ",
  "SCR_TEXT_3418": "ï¼Š There is one exception&  to the aforementioned&  rules:/",
  "SCR_TEXT_3419": "ï¼Š A certain type of monster^1,&  the \"boss\" monster./",
  "SCR_TEXT_342": "\\E2ï¼Š ãŸã—ã‹â€¦ã€€ã²ã ã‚Šã®&ã€€ ã‚¹ã‚¤ãƒƒãƒã ã£ãŸã¨&ã€€ ãŠã‚‚ã£ãŸã‘ã‚Œã©â€¦/%",
  "SCR_TEXT_3420": "ï¼Š Due to its life cycle^1, it&  possesses an incredibly&  strong soul for a monster./",
  "SCR_TEXT_3421": "ï¼Š This soul can remain&  stable after death^1, if&  only for a few moments./%%",
  "SCR_TEXT_3424": "ï¼Š (You decide not to read it.)/%%",
